<title>ISRAEL: Israeli banks lower prime rate 0.3 pct point.</title>
<headline>Israeli banks lower prime rate 0.3 pct point.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's commercial banks announced they would lower the prime rate by 0.3 percentage point to an annualised nominal rate of 17 percent.</p>
<p>The new rate will take effect on September 26.</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of Israel's announcement earlier on Tuesday that it would lower its key lending rate for October by 0.3 percentage point to 15.5 percent.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
